      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test. Key understandability issues in the original:\n1. Unused imports (`assertArrayEquals`, `assertFalse`, `assertNull`, `assertThrows`, `assertTrue`, `ByteBuffer`)\n2. Unused fixture fields (`BYTES_FIXTURE_16BE`, `BYTES_FIXTURE_16LE`, `STRING_FIXTURE`)\n3. Dead helper method `testGetBytesUnchecked` that is never called\n4. Indirect flow via `testNewString` helper obscures what the test actually verifies\n5. Variable names `expected`/`actual` repeated across both assertions without distinguishing what each assertion is checkingThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports, dead fixture fields, and the never-called `testGetBytesUnchecked` helper, inlines the `testNewString` delegate into the single `@Test` method, and uses distinct variable names (`expectedGeneric`/`actualGeneric` vs `expectedUsAscii`/`actualUsAscii`) so both assertions are immediately understandable without jumping between methods."
